This repository contains material under three different terms. Please read
which is which before reusing anything.


1. THE UNDERLYING PUBLICATION — public domain
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Elsie Clews Parsons, "Laguna Genealogies", Anthropological Papers of the
American Museum of Natural History, vol. 19, pt. 5 (1923), pp. 133-292.

Published in 1923 and therefore in the public domain in the United States.
The source scan in sources/ is a reproduction of that public-domain plate.


2. THE TRANSCRIPTION, ENCODING, CODE AND LAYOUT — CC BY 4.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright (c) 2026 Elizabeth Heger-Vlahovic

This covers scripts/, docs/, and the structured data: the character-by-character
reading of the plate, the normalised PERSONS / UNIONS / CHILDREN schema, the
editorial notes, and the code that renders the chart.

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt this material for any purpose, including commercially,
provided you give appropriate credit. Please cite both this edition and the
Parsons publication it transcribes — see CITATION.cff.


3. THE EMBEDDED TYPEFACE — SIL Open Font License 1.1
------------------------------------------------------------------------
vendor/gentium/ contains SIL Gentium 7.000, and the published pages embed a
subset of it. Gentium is copyright (c) SIL International, licensed under the
SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The full licence text is at
vendor/gentium/OFL.txt and is served at docs/fonts/OFL.txt.

"Gentium" is a Reserved Font Name under that licence. The subset shipped in
this project is a modified version and is therefore named "Laguna Serif"
instead. See scripts/subset_font.py.


A NOTE ON THE CONTENT
------------------------------------------------------------------------
This is Laguna Pueblo material. The licences above concern copyright, which is
not the only consideration that applies to Indigenous cultural heritage. Parsons
published Laguna material that members of the community regarded as restricted.
Anyone reusing this work is asked to weigh that history alongside the legal
terms.
